{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1541013-past-technocratic-limitations","id":1541013,"title":"Past technocratic limitations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-26T00:20:13-07:00","id":1541013,"title":"Past technocratic limitations","content":"Did technocrats before modern times had access to teleportation? The books say the have tech 20-40 years in advance. So would they have access to teleportation say in the 1920?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T01:06:40-07:00","id":1541015,"title":"","content":"At the cost of paradox perhaps. Maybe the Technocrats had to step sideways into secret bases to use teleportation. After all, the Void Engineers were making interstellar flights in the 1920s, so teleportation isn't really more outrageous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T09:38:44-07:00","id":1541022,"title":"","content":"What is meant by &quot;have tech 20\u201340 years in advance&quot; is more about where the line between Coincidental and Vulgar is in Technocratic Reality Zones, and basically says that if a piece of technology is a conservative extension of accepted technology, then it's Coincidental; if it isn't, then it's Vulgar. And if you're willing to use Vulgar technology, there are very few limits to what you can do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T07:58:55-07:00","id":1541530,"title":"","content":"They were able to use Teleportation in the 1400's. It was pseudoscience borderline sorcery. The Sorcerous Crusade makes it clear. In the past, the higher ups of the Order of Reason were well aware that they were full of shit.<br /> <br /> Think of it all as the many flavors of &quot;something-punk&quot;. Today they are roughly &quot;cyber-punk&quot;, but in the past they were &quot;Atom-punk&quot; (think Fallout universe), &quot;Diesel-punk&quot; (yes, both &quot;Atom-punk&quot; and &quot;Diesel-punk&quot; are indeed a thing, look it up, it's pretty cool), Steam-punk, which is the most well known and more iconic of that style of aesthetic alt-techs, but there's also the... Damn, I forgot the name. It's &quot;Renaissance-punk&quot;, that's not the name, it has a proper name, I'll Google it in a second, but basically it is an aesthetic with a &quot;Da Vincian&quot; style (there's also &quot;something-punk&quot; stuff for even previous tech levels, for example based on &quot;Archimedean tech&quot; such as mirrors and such, and even &quot;Stone-punk&quot;, Flintstones style of stone age tech).<br /> <br /> They had &quot;Da Vincian-like&quot; teleporters that ANY modern technocrat would immediately denounce as sourcery, but they used it nevertheless (and the NWO probably has erased all the blueprints of these &quot;failed projects&quot; over the eras)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T10:01:57-07:00","id":1541539,"title":"","content":"Retrofuturism is the technical name for the genre. ClockPunk is probably the most common term for pre-19th century/pre-SteamPunk settings, with RococoPunk sometimes used to differentiate 17th and 18th century ClockPunk from Rennaissance era DaVinciPunk.<br /> <br /> And yes, they'd have access to teleportation. It's just that the justification for it will be really obtuse and even convoluted, the same way things like Sorcerers Crusade Order of Reason sacred architecture was, and so extremely Vulgar. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T09:36:46-07:00","id":1541740,"title":"","content":"Others summed up the point succinctly. But I also want to point out that there are <i>levels</i> of what we might call teleportation. In the Sorcerer's Crusade, the Order of Reason had access to Connection rotes that revolved around, not so much teleporting directly to the destination, but using their understanding to make it easier and faster to get where they needed to go. Cartographers who could always find shortcuts and alternate routes that shave time off a journey. Or infiltrators who employ tools like grappling hooks, lock picks, and spiked shoes to enter buildings more effectively. These were the equivalent to Correspondence Effects, but at no point would an observer be able to tell where the Mage had &quot;cheated Reality&quot;. To the point they were rotes available to members of the &quot;Outer Labyrinth&quot; (Order of Reason members unaware Magick underpins their arts and artifice), who are relegated to largely &quot;Coincidental&quot; Effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T10:25:52-07:00","id":1541741,"title":"","content":"If you want a (very convoluted) period explanation, have advanced image dissector tubes that convert people and objects into electrical signals which are then broadcast to another location as radio waves. Most likely to some sort of already stationed receiver which converts the signal back to its original form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T09:47:37-07:00","id":1542374,"title":"","content":"Thank you all. I have a couple of follow up questions:<br /> <br /> 1. How would a technocrat in the past make a mercenary team appear on his call? (eqivalent of a sindicate member casting a spell for backup using a phone)<br /> 2. How would a technocrat in the past curse someone from far away? (like a tradition mage using the targets hair or blood)<br /> <br /> It would be helpful if you described the process and spheres needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T13:06:39-07:00","id":1542385,"title":"","content":"I made a mistake posting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-18-2024, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T09:05:26-07:00","id":1542482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1541013-past-technocratic-limitations?p=1542374#post1542374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you all. I have a couple of follow up questions:<br /> <br /> 1. How would a technocrat in the past make a mercenary team appear on his call? (eqivalent of a sindicate member casting a spell for backup using a phone)<br /> 2. How would a technocrat in the past curse someone from far away? (like a tradition mage using the targets hair or blood)<br /> <br /> It would be helpful if you described the process and spheres needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Spheres needed will never change and it will always be the same for either Trads, Techies or Prometeans.<br /> <br /> Now, just clarify something to me, what do you mean &quot;appear on his call&quot;? Like teleporting into the scene? Because if it's just calling them to show up, then it's just a simple phone call.<br /> <br /> I don't remember very well about the Sorcerer's Crusade to tell very well, I've read the book but it's not my kind of play. There are many things for the old Order of Reason that were dangerously close to sorcery and would not be more than pseudo-science today. &quot;Curses&quot; would be Entropy, at what level depends on what you're aiming for, and as for the how, I would have to take a look, but it would be stuff like &quot;Sacred Geometry&quot; and perhaps even &quot;Astrology&quot; or Alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T10:32:08-07:00","id":1542484,"title":"","content":"For the specific procedures, it is the same as today: it depends on the agent.<br /> <br /> Even the Syndicate agent may be doing a lot of different things with this \u201ccall\u201d, and can do any of those things through several other means.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re hyperfocusing on transposing modern tech and science into the past, but that\u2019s not what it is about. That\u2019s not what it is about even in the modern setting.<br /> <br /> Technocrats are Mages making shit up based on their personal beliefs, with modern technology being just a skin to their work. They try as much as they can to stay within scientific parameters, but the real science isn\u2019t the actual point.<br /> <br /> Pre-Modern Technocrats simply did shit up based on what they believed at the time, including not being limited by things they didn\u2019t knew to be impossible. The more you go into the past, the less they seem like sci-fi to us, because they\u2019re sci-fi to the proper time period. Which is still quite mystic during most of the existence of the Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> So trying to translate specific procedures, or to keep it \u201cscientific\u201d, is to lose sight of what they really are and really were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T12:34:29-07:00","id":1542492,"title":"","content":"I think you would need to look at any given period's view of the future. I can't think of any Science Fiction work I read in the 1970s that actually predicted the Internet. Remember that the Internet was being built in the 1970s! Al Gore got funding for it! (Which is why everyone had to label him a liar for stating that the Internet was his baby).<br /> <br /> Science Fiction isn't an infallible guide. But things like Popular Mechanics and Popular Science future articles are often excellent guides to past ideas of the future. I'm sixty, I have been waiting for my Air Car and Robot Housecleaner since I first saw the Jetsons. ;-)<br /> <br /> What would be seen as a possible future technology by the ordinary person on the street and what an engineer or scientist would as as probable won't tend to mesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-24-2024, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T15:39:08-07:00","id":1542499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1541013-past-technocratic-limitations?p=1542492#post1542492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been waiting for my Air Car and Robot Housecleaner since I first saw the Jetsons. ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we do have roombas today, nothing stops you from calling it &quot;Rosie&quot;.<br /> <br /> But yeah, in the end, whatever the time period of your story, Mages will be living in the &quot;future&quot;, not in the future, and the &quot;future&quot; will always have infinite potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}